# .release-removals — paths this repository used to publish and deliberately no longer does.
#
# If a file you could once fetch from here has gone, the reason belongs in this file: what moved,
# and where to look for it now. A removal is not forbidden; an unexplained one is, because from
# outside there is no way to tell a deliberate withdrawal from a mistake.
#
# One path or path-prefix per line. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored.

# ── The repository placeholder ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `temp.txt` was the single empty-repository placeholder that existed only so this
# repository had a branch before its first release was prepared. It never carried
# content, nothing referenced it, and this release replaces it with the actual tree.
# It is listed here because it WAS on the published branch, and from outside a
# vanished path cannot be told apart from a mistake — which is what this file is for.
temp.txt

# ⭐ NOTHING ELSE IS LISTED, AND THAT IS A MEASUREMENT RATHER THAN AN OVERSIGHT.
# No released version of this repository has been published yet, so apart from the
# placeholder above there is no earlier public tree for anything to have disappeared
# from. The first release adds files and withdraws nothing a reader ever used.
#
# Two things worth knowing if you are the next person here: a path that stops being published is
